meta {
  name: Assistant Email Webhook
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hooks/assistant/email?token={{assistantEmailInboundToken}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  token: {{assistantEmailInboundToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "MessageID": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "From": "jane.doe@example.com",
    "FromFull": {
      "Email": "jane.doe@example.com",
      "Name": "Jane Doe"
    },
    "ToFull": [
      {
        "Email": "orb@example.com",
        "Name": ""
      }
    ],
    "CcFull": [],
    "Subject": "Can you move my 3pm?",
    "TextBody": "Please move my 3pm call to tomorrow morning.",
    "StrippedTextReply": "",
    "Headers": []
  }
}

docs {
  Inbound email for the personal assistant, posted by the mail provider
  (Postmark-style inbound JSON). Not called by clients.

  **Auth.** No session; the `token` query string must equal
  `ASSISTANT_EMAIL_INBOUND_TOKEN` (`assistant.channels.email.inbound_token`).
  Missing or wrong token — or no token configured — answers `404`.
  Throttled to 120 per minute.

  Mail is acted on only when a `To`/`Cc` address is the assistant's
  address, the sender is a known member, and (unless
  `ASSISTANT_EMAIL_REQUIRE_AUTH` is off) the `Headers` show SPF or DKIM
  passed — so this hand-written sample is normally ignored.

  Response is **not** wrapped: `200 { "result": "<outcome>" }`, e.g.
  `ignored: not addressed to the assistant`, `ignored: unknown sender`.
}
